Z||000003||chester||08-04-2001||08:59 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>Hey hey,<BR>   Im looking into the 2" drop spindles for the front and the coil-overs for the rear. What all do I need to get or replace so all the components work together?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Street Dreams makes drop spindles that will work with the stock control arms but I think tey require 16" or bigger rims.  There are a few rear coilover setups. All work with stock components. RCC and Ground Control make rear coil over kits.<P>Rob D<P><p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 08-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Loki||08-04-2001||09:19 PM||||So up front can stayy stock  its just changing spindle? And you can use stock wills.  And for rear the coil-overs go along with the stock struts?<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000005||chester||08-05-2001||11:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>So up front can stayy stock  its just changing spindle? And you can use stock wills.  And for rear the coil-overs go along with the stock struts?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here is the link to street dreams. <A HREF="http://www.iserv.net/~strdream/dropspindles.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.iserv.net/~strdream/dropspindles.html</A>   Depends on which wheels you have for the front.  The back coilovers are conversions for the stock style struts from both RCC (they don't have a web site) and ground control racing <A HREF="http://www.ground-control.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ground-control.com/</A>  Hope this helps.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
